==Russian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|ru|вос-||before a voiceless consonant}}

===Etymology===
Traditionally explained as borrowing from Old Church Slavonic {{m|cu|въз-}}; compare inherited cognate {{doublet|ru|вз-|notext=1}}. However, there is an opinion about independent development, compare the words {{m|ru|взойти}}, {{m|ru|взобраться}}, {{m|ru|взорвать}}, which indicate the presence of a second /ъ/ in the prefix, which makes it possible to create a strong position for /ъ/ and transition to /o/. Also compare ''възогъловие'' (*възъголовие) in birch bark manuscript №469. Per Zaliznyak, prefix ''възъ-'' arose by analogy with the Old East Slavic prefixes like ''отъ-'' and ''подъ-''<ref>Andrey Zaliznyak. Drevnenovgorodskij dialekt. Jazyki slavjanskoj kul'tury: Moskva. 2004. page 360</ref>.

